{# ---------------------------------------------------------------- WHY --- #}
<section id="why" class="sas-why">
  <div class="wrap wrap--wide">
    <div class="sas-why-grid">
      <div class="sas-why-fig">
        <div class="sas-why-num" data-count="95" data-suffix="%">95%</div>
        <div class="sas-why-fig-label">of the value of any strategy lies in its delivery.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sas-why-body">
        <div class="eyebrow">Why</div>
        <h2>Creating a strategy was never the hard part.</h2>
        <p>The workshops, the vision statement, the roadmap &mdash; pulling people out of their day-to-day and giving them room to think generates real energy. Teams enjoy it.</p>
        <p>The hard part is what happens in month four, and month ten, and month sixteen, when that energy fades and the daily pressure of running the business reasserts itself. That&rsquo;s where most strategies quietly die &mdash; leaving a failed investment and a team more skeptical of the next initiative than before.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Illustrative, not data: where energy goes after the deck. #}
    <figure class="sas-energy" aria-labelledby="energy-cap">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1000 230" role="img" aria-label="Illustration: after the strategy deck, momentum in a traditional engagement fades by month four, ten and sixteen; with weekly delivery support it is sustained to the finish.">
